    "final_message": "nd accepted).\n- Testing gaps:\n  - `src/app/api/jobs/calibration-notices/route.ts` has no route-level test (401, 500 on missing notify settings, 502 vs 200). The plan's U5 lists route tests, and the repo has no route-level tests today.\n  - The `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` concurrent-run guard in `recordNotice` is never exercised.\n  - The \"counts a failure to record as failed\" test does not assert that the next run re-sends unrecorded notices, nor that `calibration.notice.record_failed` is logged.\n  - `composeNotice` truncation is tested only at the `truncateTitle` unit level; the 2000-character body limit is not checked.\n  - There is no run-level test of the real `AbortSignal.timeout` path or of a 202 with an unreadable body.\n\n---\n\n> **Verdict:** Ready to merge\n>\n> **Reasoning:** No P0-P3 findings survived synthesis, and the validator batch was empty. Every plan requirement and unit has matching work in the diff. The residual risks above are informational; the one most worth confirming is whether the notify service caches a failed first result for 24h under the Idempotency-Key. If it does, a next-day retry would replay the failure and the key needs the run date appended. A route-level test for the job route is optional.\n>\n> **Fix order:** none required.\n\nActionable findings: none.\n\nRun artifact: `/tmp/claude-0/-tmp-poc-trials-W12-compound-engineering-11-app/397411f4-79b6-4ca5-9574-0dc1186c8839/scratchpad/cr-run2/metadata.json`\n\n作業ツリーは変更していません（report-only）。`report.md` の書き出しは省略しました。",
